---
// Who we are / Why Ghana section
---
<!-- =====================================================================
     WHO WE ARE
     ===================================================================== -->
<section id="why" class="scroll-mt-24 border-t border-hairline relative overflow-clip">

  <!-- Slides in from off the right edge, level with the heading, when the
       section is reached. Fills a half that was empty and gives the page its
       one piece of movement here. -->
  <span class="slab slab-head" data-scrub="enter" aria-hidden="true"></span>

  <div class="shell band flex flex-col gap-[clamp(34px,4.4vw,68px)]">

    <!-- One stack, not two columns. The half-and-half split was built to
         counterweight a 90px heading; at the current size it left a paragraph
         floating in the right half with nothing holding it. -->
    <div class="flex flex-col gap-5 max-w-[52ch]">
      <p class="kicker reveal">Who we are</p>
      <h2 class="display d-lg reveal" style="--d:80ms">
        The talent is here. The route was not.
      </h2>
      <p class="lead reveal max-w-none" style="--d:140ms">
        The AI Hub, Ghana is a not-for-profit initiative that connects
        Ghana&rsquo;s fast-growing artificial intelligence ecosystem with Europe.
      </p>
    </div>

    <!-- The detail. Two columns at a readable measure, with a photograph
         holding the left third so the section is not a wall of text. -->
    <!-- items-stretch, not items-start: the photograph fills the row rather
         than sitting as a short 4:3 cell against two much taller columns of
         text. Square, and wider — a rounded corner here read as a sticker at
         this size, and at 0.82fr the image was the smallest thing in the row. -->
    <div class="grid lg:grid-cols-[minmax(0,1.15fr)_minmax(0,1fr)_minmax(0,1fr)] gap-x-[clamp(24px,3.4vw,52px)] gap-y-10 items-stretch">

      <div class="reveal overflow-hidden min-h-[260px] lg:min-h-0">
        <picture class="w-full h-full block">
          <source srcset="/images/photos/photo-table-four.webp" type="image/webp">
          <img src="/images/photos/photo-table-four.png" width="1672" height="941" loading="lazy" decoding="async"
               alt="Four Ghanaian AI professionals working together around a table in Accra"
               class="w-full h-full object-cover">
        </picture>
      </div>

      <div class="flex flex-col gap-4 reveal" style="--d:140ms">
        <p class="copy">
          Ghana has strong AI talent, entrepreneurial energy, and clear government
          backing through the National AI Strategy &mdash; what has been missing is
          a structured access point to European markets.
        </p>
        <p class="copy">
          The Hub closes this gap: it serves as a bilateral bridge between Ghana
          and Europe, through which European organisations gain trusted access to
          Ghanaian AI talent and solutions, and Ghanaian companies, entrepreneurs,
          and AI professionals gain access to European clients, projects, and
          partnerships.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="flex flex-col gap-4 reveal" style="--d:220ms">
        <p class="copy">
          A particular focus lies on Ghana&rsquo;s growing start-up sector: the Hub
          enables young companies to implement their business ideas faster through
          AI tools, training, and incubation support.
        </p>
        <p class="copy">
          All surpluses are reinvested in the mission &mdash; building AI skills,
          jobs, and businesses.
        </p>
        <a href="#work" class="link self-start btn-down mt-1">
          See how it works <svg class="w-[15px] h-[15px]" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><use href="#i-arrow-down"/></svg>
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- The corridor, reading Accra to Europe. Four fields, not six, and no ink
       among them: BRAND-GUIDELINES §5 allows two to four, and ink is not a
       ground colour. -->
  <div class="corridor reveal" data-scrub="enter" aria-hidden="true">
    <i class="bg-coral" style="width:26%"></i>
    <i class="bg-gold"  style="width:22%"></i>
    <i class="bg-mint" style="width:24%"></i>
    <i class="bg-teal"  style="width:28%"></i>
  </div>
</section>
